                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Purrfect Date - the very well written odd dating sim. Downsides - it's missing key components necessary for a visual novel. You can't skip text you've read before, you can't save at a decision point so it is easy to backtrack, forced autosave, requires multiple playthroughs to get all achievements. (like no dating cats/cats dump you/you reject cat feelings). Cute notes: Music is adorable if a bit repetitive. Artwork is playful and fun. Writing is excellent. But the lack of standard visual novel features kills my drive to play for more endings. Too much button pressing for content I've already read.",
